		<p class="Text_ind" style="margin:0;padding:0;border-width:0;font-family:Times New Roman PS Std, serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;margin-top:8pt;orphans:2;page-break-after:auto;page-break-before:auto;text-align:justify;text-indent:24pt;widows:3;margin-top:7pt;margin-top:7pt;">Research and development revenue decreased by 13.1%, or approximately $0.8<span class="nobreak"> </span>million, for the three months ended March<span class="nobreak"> </span>31, 2023, as compared to the three months ended March<span class="nobreak"> </span>31, 2022, primarily due to decreased research and development work performed pursuant to the BARDA Burn II contract. New patient enrollments in our BARDA clinical study decreased in the three months ended March<span class="nobreak"> </span>31, 2023 compared to the three months ended March<span class="nobreak"> </span>31, 2022 as the Company is completing enrollment and transitioning to the closeout phase of the study.</p>
